 "assessment": {
  "name": "MASCC Unmet Needs Assessment for Cancer-Related Cognitive Impairment Impact (MASCC COG-IMPACT)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Multinational Association for Supportive Care in Cancer (MASCC) Unmet Needs Assessment of Cancer-Related Cognitive Impairment Impact (MASCC COG-IMPACT) is a 55-item self-report measure developed by Haywood and colleagues (2025) under the auspices of MASCC. It is designed for adults aged 18 and over who have completed curative-intent cancer treatment, have no current evidence of disease, and who self-identify as experiencing cancer-related cognitive impairment (CRCI).",
